      "notes": "Verdict is well-structured and internally consistent. All claims are appropriately tiered and quotes entail the claims as stated. The tier for E6-backed claim ('grants will be paid on top of loans without increasing debt') is marked 'projected' \u2014 this is a mild over-caution since E6 states it as a government commitment, but it's defensible as a forward-looking policy effect rather than a measured fact. The E13 claim on '80% less in real terms' is sourced to IF (advocacy), which is labelled in sources; this is a warning-level concern but not blocking since the verdict does not rely solely on it and the broader picture is corroborated. The 'stated' claim for E5 (year-2 grant amounts) is drawn from a government policy document rather than the party's own manifesto text, making it technically a measurable or stated-from-government rather than from the policy text itself \u2014 minor but not blocking. Direction 'improves' is justified and not false-balanced; the verdict correctly acknowledges limitations without manufacturing balance. Magnitude 'minor' and confidence 'moderate' are well-supported. No lever leakage, no party identity signals."
    },
